.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1036 AM PST Fri Nov 20 2026

Lingering rain showers continue to stream across the South Bay into
the Central Coast. These should be the last bit of shower activity
before another (weak) cold front arrives late Saturday morning with
more rain. VFR conditions prevail through the TAF cycle, however
brief reductions in visibility may occur with moderate shower
activity early this afternoon. Moderate south to easterly winds up
to 10-15 kt persist into the evening with a few bursts of
northwesterly flow at select terminals. Low confidence on fog
development early Saturday morning at KSTS due to the approaching
cold front. The current TAF hints at the possibility of lower
ceilings and reduced visibility, however high clouds ahead of the
front (and the expected rainfall) should limit fog development.

Enjoy the *brief* period of dryness aviators!

Vicinity of SFO...VFR with SE-E winds persist and peak around 10-15
kt this afternoon. Ceilings begin to lower Saturday morning as the
cold front nears the terminals with moderate confidence for VFR to
persist. Low confidence on exactly when rain showers will arrive at
the terminals on Saturday, though current model guidance suggests
some time between 21Z Sat to 01Z Sun.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...Light rain showers persist into the early
afternoon with brief MVFR conditions possible. Otherwise, VFR
through the TAF period with occasional bursts of NW flow. Overnight,
southeasterly breezes prevail with lower (VFR) ceilings Saturday
morning. Moderate winds around 10 kt are also likely at SNS early
Saturday morning.

